quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  18,46,"Wealth and children are the attractions of the worldly life. However, the everlasting righteous deeds are better in reward with your Lord and better in hope."
  18,47,"On the Day when We shall make the mountains move away, and you will see the earth an open plain, and We shall gather them, We shall not leave any of them out."
  18,48,"And they will be presented before your Lord in rows. (It will be said to them:) ‘Indeed, you have come to Us as We created you the first time. Rather, you claimed that We would never appoint for you a time for the fulfilment of the promise.’"
  18,49,"The record of deeds will be laid (open). Then, you will see the evildoers fearful of what is in it. They will say: ‘Oh, woe to us! What kind of record is this that does not omit anything, small or big, but numbers them all.’ And they will find present whatsoever they had done. And your Lord does not deal with anyone unjustly."
  18,50,"And (remember) when We said to the angels: ‘Prostrate before Adam (in veneration).’ So they prostrated except Iblis. He was one of the jinn, so he deviated from the command of his Lord. Would you still take him and his offspring as guardians besides Me, though they are your enemies? How evil an exchange for the wrongdoers!"
  18,51,"I did not make them witnesses to the creation of the heavens and the earth, nor their own creation. And I do not take the misleaders as assistants."
  18,52,"On the Day, He will say: ‘Call those whom you claimed as My partners.’ They will call upon them, but they will not respond to them, and We will cause a destructive separation between them."
  18,53,"The evildoers will see the Fire and will realise that they are about to fall into it, and they will find no means of escape from it."
